  "cause": "**Ukraine put seven naval drones into a Libyan port and sank one of Russia's newest warships while it refuelled, and the operation was planned to be seen.** On **Sunday morning** an explosion struck a warship docked at the **Benghazi naval base** in eastern Libya; the **Government of National Stability**, the eastern administration, said the vessel had stopped for fuel and supplies on its way back to Russia under an existing maritime agreement. On **Monday** President **Zelensky** gave the account himself: **seven naval drones** were deployed to target and sink the corvette **Merkury**, a **Project 20380 Steregushchiy-class** ship he called one of Russia's newest, and a **Ka-27** combat helicopter was also destroyed. He named a second target, the **MV ANGARA**, a Russian container carrier he said was transporting weapons. Commercial satellite imagery is consistent with the claim — **Vantor** released high-resolution images showing the corvette moored on Saturday and, on Sunday, capsized with only the bow above water; **Planet Labs** imagery showed a vessel on fire at the port at **05:47 GMT**, and **BBC Verify** geolocated video of the burning ship. Eastern Libya's health ministry said it had received injured people from a commercial ship struck off the port, and the UN mission, **UNSMIL**, expressed *\"serious concern\"* and demanded an *\"immediate, independent and transparent investigation\"*: *\"Libya cannot afford, and must not become a battleground for foreign conflicts.\"* The strike came one day after the **Sparta II** was hit in the **Gulf of Finland** — Finland's defence forces said Ukraine was likely responsible — and as a Russian strike on **Dymer** in Ukraine killed **eleven** people, among them a **seven-year-old boy** pulled alive from the rubble hours later.",
