  "cause": "**The longest climate conference in the history of the United Nations ended on Sunday with no agreement at all, over the absence of two words.** **COP31** in **Antalya**, jointly hosted by **Turkey** and **Australia**, ran past its Friday deadline into Sunday and became the longest UN climate summit ever held; the closing plenary failed to adopt the **\"Antalya Pacts\"**. The final draft, circulated in the early hours of Sunday, contained no occurrence of *fossil fuels*; its only reference to coal, oil and gas was an indirect nod to the **COP28** pledge to *\"transition away\"* from them. A first draft on Monday had used the term **six times** — and that was unacceptable to oil-producing states. The **EU's** representative, Irish minister **Darragh O'Brien**, said the EU objected *\"strongly\"* and that the decisions *\"go nowhere near the level of ambition needed\"*: *\"It is unconscionable that we would have a climate pact that makes no mention of fossil fuels.\"* **Panama** and the **Marshall Islands** joined the objection, and poorer states protested the absence of any clear financial commitment from wealthy nations on adaptation. **UN Secretary-General António Guterres**, at his last COP before stepping down, said he was *\"deeply disappointed\"* and aimed at *\"powerful fossil fuel interests\"* who were taking *\"a page from Big Tobacco's playbook: distorting the science, delaying policy, blocking action, and piling up huge profits while people everywhere pay the price.\"* Australia's Prime Minister **Anthony Albanese**, whose country co-hosted, blamed *\"difficult geopolitical times\"*; UK Energy Secretary **Miatta Fahnbulleh** said the summit had *\"sought to confront hard truths — that global warming is set to overshoot 1.5C\"*. The last comparable collapse of a COP's central political agreement was **Copenhagen in 2009**. This was also the first COP convened since the UN warned that global temperatures are expected to exceed **1.5°C** above pre-industrial levels; the discarded draft had proposed carbon dioxide removal, never before named in a COP decision. The next summit is in **Addis Ababa** in November 2027.",
