   "**The instrument that failed is consensus, and it failed exactly as designed** — a room of nearly two hundred delegations where a single producer's objection is sufficient, and where the objection was made and sustained; the direct effect is that the most consequential text of the decade was decided by its least willing signatory; the compound consequence is that every future COP now knows the price of a holdout is total, which makes intransigence the highest-return strategy in the building and turns the plenary into a hostage exchange",
   "**Two deleted words are worth more than the whole document that survived them** — six mentions in Monday's draft, zero on Sunday, and the collapse that followed; the direct effect is that the parties have now demonstrated, on the record, what they will and will not write; the compound consequence is that the deletion is the only durable output of Antalya, because it is the one thing every delegation has agreed to by walking out",
   "**No deal is not the absence of a signal; it is a very clear one, and the market reads it faster than the diplomats** — Copenhagen 2009 followed by a decade of falling clean-energy costs shows what actually moved emissions; the direct effect is that Antalya removes the coordination signal and leaves the capital signal intact; the compound consequence is that investment continues where the economics work and stalls where policy support was the only reason to build — which is precisely the hard-to-abate sector the text was supposed to address",
