  "verse": "To your human sense and your human view are also connected your earthly jurisdictions, but you must not expect that these are equivalent with the strength of the character and of all virtues of the Creation Universal Consciousness nor with the Creation-given laws and recommendations to which your earthly courts and their laws do not even get close; exactly the opposite is the case, because between your understanding of the fairness and of the creational fairness there is generally in the true sense of the word a scandalous and shaking difference.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 372",
  "hinge": "§28:372 is not a dismissal of courts. It is a warning about **what a court can be mistaken for** — the text says the gap between human jurisdiction and creational fairness is *\"scandalous and shaking\"*, which cuts against both the cynic who says the ruling is worthless and the enthusiast who says justice has now been done. A final judgment is a true statement about the past that cannot by itself alter the present; what alters the present is what states do with it. **First,** convert the compensation obligation into **a mechanism**: a quantified sum, a schedule, a named custodian, and asset or recognition leverage attached to non-payment — otherwise the ruling is a monument. **Second,** make the **Rohingya party to the remedy**, not its subject: camps, returns and citizenship are decided in negotiations where they currently have no standing, and a claim they cannot spend is not restitution. **Third,** use the **precedent deliberately and narrowly** — cite the evidentiary standard where it fits and refuse to inflate it where it does not, because a precedent over-claimed is a precedent that gets distinguished away, and this one is too rare to waste."
